1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roaring]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words…

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called…

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

12
00:01:59,000 --> 00:01:59,000
[Gon] Now!

13
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
I did it!

14
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,000
I figured it out!

15
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
I’ve just gotta go for the target

16
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
the moment it goes for its prey!

17
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
EXPLOSION x OF x DECEPTION

18
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
[birds chirping]

19
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
[narrator] Zevil Island, day two.

20
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Gon has mastered the technique

21
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
that will be instrumental
in the capture of his target.

22
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,000
[winces in pain]

23
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Ow! My hands are all bloody.

24
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Well… I guess

25
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
I have been casting my fishing rod
for two straight days.

26
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Still all that practice
has really paid off.

27
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Now when a bird swoops down on a fish,

28
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
I can snag it every time.

29
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
If I use it the right way,

30
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
I’ll be able to steal Hisoka’s badge.

31
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
All that’s left now is to find him!

32
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
[grunts in pain]

33
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
But how am I supposed
to find Hisoka, anyway?

34
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
I guess I’ll just have to walk around

35
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
and trust my instincts to guide me.

36
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
What the--?

37
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Why are they all gathering around me
like that?

38
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Hm...

39
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
I think these butterflies

40
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
are attracted to the smell of blood.

41
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
[walkie-talkie beeping]

42
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
[Gitarrackur] Have you taken
your target’s badge, Hisoka?

43
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
[Hisoka] No, not yet.

44
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
You don’t even know
who your target is yet, do you?

45
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,000
[Hisoka] No.

46
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
[Gitarrackur] Want me to tell you?

47
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
[Hisoka] No. It doesn’t matter.

48
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
I’ll just hunt down three others.

49
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:29,000
[Gon] If I remember right,
Hisoka was injured back at the tower.

50
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
If this works,

51
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
these butterflies
might lead me right to him

52
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
It’s the guy who got shot with the arrow.

53
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
[birds chirping]

54
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Oh, well. Better luck next year.

55
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
There he is!

56
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
[tense breathing]

57
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
[tense breathing]

58
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,000
[Gon] Calm down…

59
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Calm down!

60
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
[tense breathing]

61
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,000
[exhales, relaxed]

62
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
I’ll just have to wait…

63
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,000
until he makes his move.

64
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,000
[Leorio Paradinight] Dammit.

65
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Where the hell is everybody hiding?

66
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
It’s been two days,

67
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,000
and I haven’t seen anyone.

68
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
-[rustling]
-[gasps]

69
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Who’s there?

70
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,000
[Tonpa] Whoa, hold on!

71
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
It’s just me, okay?

72
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
[Leorio] Tonpa!

73
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
So, I’m your target.

74
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
[Tonpa] Hey, wait a minute! Just relax!

75
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:59,000
I promise you’re not my target, all right?

76
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Then prove it.

77
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Right. Uh...

78
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,000
See?

79
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Hmm...

80
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
[relieved sigh]

81
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
I guess it’s a good thing
I didn’t throw it away, huh?

82
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
There’s no point
in going after just anyone.

83
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
That’s a huge waste of time and energy.

84
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Wait, wait, wait, wait…

85
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Don’t tell me.
I’m not your target… am I?

86
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
Unfortunately, you’re not.

87
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[Tonpa] Two-forty-six.

88
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Ponzu, huh?

89
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
[gasps]
Wait, are you saying you know who that is?

90
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Are you saying you didn’t?

91
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Oh, well, see, uh…

92
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
I wouldn’t put it like that.

93
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
I just didn’t have the chance
to figure it out yet.

94
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,000
[smirks]

95
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Do you want me to fill you in?

96
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
What?

97
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,000
[Tonpa]
What they look like, their weapons,

98
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
their special abilities,
and their weaknesses?

99
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
I will.

100
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
But I have one condition.

101
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
[rumbling]

102
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,000
Hm?

103
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:05,000
[Tonpa] I ate some nuts
that aren’t really agreeing with me.

104
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Nuts, you say?

105
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
To be honest,
I can barely stand right now.

106
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
But you are pre-med, aren’t you?

107
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Do you happen to have
any medicine on hand?

108
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
[upset tummy groan]

109
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
[Leorio] Whoa! Don’t crap your pants.

110
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Antidiarrheals and pretty much
all the other basics.

111
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
That’s great! Thank you!

112
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
-Huh?
-But first, the info.

113
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Fine. If you insist.

114
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:38,000
[Tonpa] For starters, Ponzu’s a woman.

115
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Go on…

116
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:44,000
[Tonpa] As far as I know,
out of the 24 applicants who are left,

117
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:48,000
there are only five of them who use
some sort of chemical weapons.

118
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Ponzu is one of ‘em.

119
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
That’s her…

120
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
She happens to specialize
in all sorts of toxins,

121
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
so you’ll want to be careful.

122
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
However, her strategy’s simple.

123
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,000
She just lies in wait.

124
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
[Leorio] She does?

125
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
She sets a trap and waits patiently
for her target to wander into it.

126
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
I see…

127
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
And you don’t have to worry
about anything else.

128
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
She’s not all that daunting herself,

129
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:18,000
so get her into an actual fight
and you’re guaranteed to win.

130
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
-[stomach rumbling]
-[Tonpa groans]

131
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
[Tonpa]
Still, if you find her, watch your step.

132
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
And remember to stay downwind.

133
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
She knows someone’s targeting her,

134
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
so it’s not like you can rely
on the element of surprise.

135
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
-[stomach rumbling]
-[grunts]

136
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
And that’s pretty much it.

137
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Now gimme that medicine!

138
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
[Leorio] Okay.

139
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,000
But I need you to take a step back.

140
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
[groans] Just hurry!

141
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
I-- I can’t hold it in!

142
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,000
-[rustling]
-[gasps]

143
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Dammit!

144
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
[Sommy chuckles]

145
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Looks like I got your badge. Heh.

146
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
I knew you were keeping it
in your briefcase.

147
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Tonpa! You’re working together?

148
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[Tonpa] You bet.

149
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
And I didn’t need your medicine.

150
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
I’ve got my own.

151
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
As you might’ve guessed,

152
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
you really were my target this whole time.

153
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
But the card you just showed me...

154
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Oh. That one’s my target.

155
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
And this one is Tonpa’s.

156
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
We traded for this little deception.

157
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
I just can’t believe you fell for it!

158
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
So, there you have it!

159
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
[yells] Damn you!

160
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
You're gonna pay for this!

161
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,000
[Tonpa] Whoops! [chuckles]

162
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Tonpa! Let’s meet at the rendezvous point!

163
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
[Tonpa] Gotcha!

164
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,000
[Leorio] Stop right there!

165
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
You’re dead, ya hear me?

166
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Why are you chasing me?

167
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
I’m not the one who’s got your badge!

168
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,000
Shut your trap!

169
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,000
You’re kidding me.

170
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,000
You still don’t get it, do ya, rookie?
That’s a shame.

171
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,000
What did you say?

172
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
It’s not our fault you got duped, buddy!

173
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
[growling]

174
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Besides, forming alliances
is a great way to pass the Exam!

175
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
I can accept the latter

176
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,000
but never the former.

177
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
[groans]

178
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
[grunts]

179
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Deception is the fault of the deceiver!

180
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Kurapika!

181
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Leorio. Would you like to team up?

182
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:43,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

183
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:47,000
TARGET

184
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:52,000
[rustling]

185
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
[squeaking]

186
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
PLEASE DO NOT FEED

187
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
-[Tonpa snorts]
-[mice squeaking]

188
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,000
[Leorio] Hey!

189
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Give me back my damn badge!

190
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
[laughing]

191
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
-If you want it, you gotta catch me!
-[monkey chatters]

192
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
[gasps]

193
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
[monkey chatters]

194
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[squealing]

195
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,000
[Leorio] Okay!

196
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
I got my badge back safe and sound!

197
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,000
We have the badges
for numbers 16 and 118, as well.

198
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:46,000
So, hey. It was pretty lucky
that Tonpa was your target.

199
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,000
You saved me back there.

200
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
[Kurapika] Please, no thanks necessary.

201
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
I didn’t want Tonpa to realize I was there

202
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:55,000
which is why I hid
while you were ambushed from behind.

203
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,000
What?

204
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
[Kurapika] In my defense,

205
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
I had to be sure
you could handle an attack like that.

206
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Otherwise, what use
would you be to me as a partner?

207
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
You qualified, though barely.

208
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
[Leorio] You are so full of it…

209
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Either way,

210
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:13,000
I admit, it’s a lot easier
when you join forces.

211
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,000
The next four days, let’s stick together.

212
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,000
All right.

213
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Well, you got your target’s badge,
so that’s a good start.

214
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Add it to your own
and that’s a total of six points.

215
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
That’s assuming he doesn’t take it back.

216
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:32,000
And number 118's badge is only worth
one more point for either of us.

217
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,000
[Leorio] True.

218
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
But it might still come in handy.

219
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
All right. We need to find your target.

220
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Number 246. Ponzu, right?

221
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,000
We need to stay alert.

222
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,000
[Kurapika] You’re telling me that?

223
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
[Leorio] Right, point taken.

224
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
[sighs]

225
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
You’ve been following me since we started.

226
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
It’s pretty damn obvious.

227
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
You wanna play?

228
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Come on out.

229
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,000
[sighs]

230
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Well? Show yourself.

231
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Hm?

232
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
I know you’re there.

233
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Did he notice me?

234
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:24,000
If you won’t come out,
I suppose I’ll have to come to you.

235
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
[Gon] This is it.

236
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
It’s all or nothing.

237
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Huh?

238
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,000
When did he--

239
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,000
[groans quietly]

240
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,000
I seek a bout with you.

241
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,000
You’ll die.

242
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,000
[grunts]

243
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Now’s my chance!

244
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Ha!

245
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
[roars]

246
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
[Gon] It’s about to happen…

247
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:30,000
I’ve just got to wait
‘til he goes for the kill!

248
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,000
[roaring]

249
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:39,000
[Goz grunting]

250
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Why?

251
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Why isn’t Hisoka fighting back?

252
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
[loud roar]

253
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[Goz panting]

254
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
I don’t get it…

255
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Why... won’t you fight?

256
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
I only need to evade

257
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
and you’ll die eventually, yes?

258
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,000
[gasps]

259
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:18,000
I can tell by
the large swarm of Hemotropic butterflies

260
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
that your wounds are quite serious.

261
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,000
[groans]

262
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:27,000
[Hisoka]
Someone has already wounded you. Correct?

263
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:31,000
I understand wanting to end your life
fighting as a warrior.

264
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
[Goz] If that’s true…
and you really do understand...

265
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,000
then why?

266
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Why do you refuse to fight me
and grant me the death I desire?

267
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Because I have no interest in the dead.

268
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,000
[Goz] Wait, what?

269
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
But I’m-- I’m not--

270
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
[Hisoka]
Do you know how I know you’re dead?

271
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Your eyes.

272
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,000
[Goz groans]

273
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Bye-bye.

274
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,000
[Goz straining]

275
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,000
[roaring]

276
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,000
[groans]

277
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,000
[gasps]

278
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,000
[Gitarrackur] Sorry.

279
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
I was careless and he got away.

280
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,000
[Hisoka] Don’t lie to me.

281
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:38,000
He probably begged you to grant him
a last request and you relented.

282
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Am I right?

283
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
[Gitarrackur]
Well, I may have felt sorry for the man.

284
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
He was going to die anyway.

285
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:50,000
You really need to stop pitying those
who serve no purpose.

286
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
But you’re guilty of that yourself.

287
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
You’ve walked away from opponents
before finishing them.

288
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,000
[Hisoka] I do have standards.

289
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Why waste time on people
who are utterly useless?

290
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:05,000
I only spare those
whose premature deaths would be a waste.

291
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Well? What about his badge?

292
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,000
Oh, I already took it.

293
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
I have six points now,

294
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
so I don’t really need this one.

295
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Want it?

296
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,000
[Hisoka] Whose is this?

297
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,000
[Gitarrackur] It belonged to someone
who tried to snipe me.

298
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,000
That pissed me off, and so...

299
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
well, I killed ‘em.

300
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Well.

301
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Hmm... That’s always so much fun to watch.

302
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:53,000
[Gitarrackur]
It does take its toll on me, you know.

303
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Ah. That’s much better.

304
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:12,000
Well, I’m gonna sleep until the deadline.

305
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Best of luck.

306
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
It got dark really quick.

307
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
We shouldn’t let our guard down.

308
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Nightfall is the best time for an ambush.

309
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,000
I know, I know.

310
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[Hisoka] Only two points left to go.

311
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:59,000
I guess I’d better start hunting.

312
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,000
This is it!

313
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,000
Hmm...

314
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Hm...

315
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Look who it is.

316
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[narrator]
Hisoka targets Kurapika and Leorio,

317
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
unaware that Gon is after his badge.

318
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:55,000
Four days remain
before the end of the Fourth Phase.

319
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Defeat x and x Disgrace"!

320
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:30,000
-Let’s shake hands!
-[Hisoka] With a nice, firm grip.
